      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the advice. the cool water helped a bit but now it's just throbbing and it feels so hot to the touch. honestly i'm a bit scared to go to the doctor because of the cost and the wait times. i read online that tea tree oil is a super strong natural antiseptic and can help heal skin wounds fast. if i just use a high concentration of that, wouldn't that be better than going to a clinic? i really feel like i can manage this at home with the right natural stuff.",
